{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>One unleavened cake of hallah.</b> It is one loaf of bread. And it is possible that ככר is a weight, and it is not the same weight as silver and gold." "<b>And he placed it on the fats.</b> And he did not mention the appendage of the liver and the kidneys, because the appendage is small, and the meaning of the word is like 'What profit has a man' (Ecclesiastes 1:3), and the kidneys are upon their fats, for it is not possible that the kidneys be called חלב; only the tail-fat is חלב."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:05.494342582Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}